{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/894699-i-designing-a-few-packs-for-nyc-any-advice","id":894699,"title":"I designing a few packs for NYC any advice","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-20T07:11:05-07:00","id":894699,"title":"I designing a few packs for NYC any advice","content":"I've never designed a werewolf back before I wanted to know if I could get some advice on creating werewolf packs. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T07:27:34-07:00","id":894706,"title":"","content":"Basically, I'd normally start with a central conceit for the pack that defines who and what they are. Something like &quot;expansionist Pure pack&quot; or &quot;friendly spiritual pack&quot;. Then I'll give the group a name and then figure out how big I want the pack to be in the story. So, with the Pure pack, if I want them to be a constant threat, I'd give them a large number of werewolf pack members. Conversely, the spiritual pack if I wanted them to serve a mentor role might only have a couple members. From there, I'll give the group some names and a few notable character traits. Hopefully by this point I have enough packs to populate the are the players are going to begin play in. <br /> <br /> From there, I tend to expand the setting as needed. Personally I generally find having every werewolf in an area named more work than what you need at the start of a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:09:18-07:00","id":894935,"title":"","content":"Packs generally base themselves after a motif. Bikers, Cops, Software Company, Firefighter prescint, a farmstead and their hands, the mob, a street-gang, etc, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> In Chicago one of the alpha packs was basically a real estate firm, which purchased properties and then used feng-shui to shape the shadow of their ever growing territory.<br /> <br /> Another example was one which ran a Dojo;<br /> <br /> Another could be a group of modern primitive hobos;<br /> <br /> Another ran a funerary home;<br /> <br /> Another could basically run a hospital.<br /> <br /> Whichever human organization you can conceive off, a pack <br /> <br /> Keep in mind, packs now got Wolfbloods and humans there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-20-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}